  "result": "The node does not pass: the gate returns **WITNESS_FAIL**, and nothing in the rule or the witnesses can fix it. The run's reading says no road-user class is definitely an authorized emergency vehicle.\n\n**What I wrote**\n- **Rule:**\n  - The subject must be in the aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle`.\n  - The rule applies except when the subject's warning lamp is flashing or rotating, in any of the four colours.\n  - The obligation is that the subject's siren is not sounding.\n  - The node left no reading open, so I declared no narrowings.\n- **Witnesses:** one vehicle driving east for three seconds, with its siren and lamps set as each of the five scenarios describes.\n\n**Why it fails**\nThe reading puts no class in that aggregate as definitely included, and lists every vehicle class (emergency vehicle, fire apparatus, motor vehicle and the rest) as unresolved. So whether a vehicle belongs to the aggregate is never true, and for any vehicle it is unknown:\n- `forbid` and `permit` come out unknown, so they can never be violated or compliant.\n- `idle` comes out unknown too, because a private passenger car is a motor vehicle, which is also unresolved.\n- `blind` is unknown because of the aggregate, not because the siren is masked.\n- `branch_1` passes, because the flashing lamps switch the rule off.\n\n**What needs to change:** the reading should include at least the emergency-vehicle and fire-apparatus classes in this aggregate. The `idle` subject also needs to be definitely outside it: either the motor-vehicle class is classified as excluded or covered, or the scenario uses something like a pedestrian or bicycle. The details are in `task_result.md`.\n\n**A mistake on my part:** my first gate call wasn't the exact allowed command. I added a pipe that threw away its output, and it ran on the unedited skeleton. It probably used one of the six runs; I noted this in `task_result.md`. I ran the gate once more, correctly, and stopped there, since more runs can't change the verdict.\n\nFiles are in `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/NRS_484D_400_5`:\n- task_result.md",
